orow(334, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MOSES CAME" (32:44) — HERE IT SAYS "AND MOSES CAME" AND THERE "AND MOSES WENT" (31:1): ONE CANNOT SAY "CAME" SINCE "WENT" IS SAID, NOR "WENT" SINCE "CAME" IS SAID — SAY THEN: HIS SUCCESSOR CAME, AND THE AUTHORITY WAS GIVEN INTO ANOTHER\'S HAND. ({SP_(334, 1, "נאמר", "כאן", "ויבא", "משה", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "it is said here and Moses came, and it is said there"; {SP_(334, 1, "בא", "דיותיכוס", "שלו")} "his successor came"; {SP_(334, 1, "והרשות", "נתנה", "ביד", "אחר")} "and the authority was given into another hand"): 31:1\'s WENT READ WITH 32:44\'s CAME — two texts set against each other and resolved by inference (the successor; the middah checked in MIDDOT.md at the manifest before its code is typed): the compile: Joshua\'s office effective at 31:1 (Moses\' going the handing over; the successor the Greek loan diadochos in the Hebrew row); the row from Haazinu\'s close (334, on 32:44) read here for 31:1, the piska not opened. Fresh.')
orow(345, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MOSES COMMANDED US TORAH" (33:4) — DO WE HOLD THE TORAH FROM MOSES OUR MASTER? OUR FATHERS MERITED IT — "THE HERITAGE OF THE CONGREGATION OF JACOB"; AN INHERITANCE FOR THE SONS OF KINGS — WHENCE FOR THE SONS OF THE SMALL? "YOU STAND THIS DAY, ALL OF YOU" (29:9). ANOTHER WORD: READ NOT "HERITAGE" (MORASHAH) BUT "BETROTHED" (ME\'ORASAH) — THE TORAH IS BETROTHED TO ISRAEL AND A MARRIED WOMAN TO THE NATIONS OF THE WORLD ("CAN A MAN TAKE FIRE IN HIS BOSOM AND HIS CLOTHES NOT BURN?", Proverbs 6:27-29). ({SP_(345, 2, "ירשה", "לבני", "קטנים", "מנין")} "an inheritance for the sons of the small — whence"; {SP_(345, 2, "אל", "תהי", "קורא", "מורשה", "אלא", "מאורסה")} "read not heritage but betrothed"): 29:9 THE PROOF THAT THE TORAH IS EVERY ISRAELITE\'S INHERITANCE (48:9\'s twin use of the verse — all of you standing); the row from Vezot Habrachah\'s piska (345, on 33:4) read here for 29:9, the piska not opened; the compile: no law — a status (the Torah\'s holders all Israel). The Writings\' seat cited (Proverbs 6:27-29), never read. Fresh.')
orow(357, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MOSES DIED THERE" (34:5) — COULD MOSES HAVE DIED AND WRITTEN "AND MOSES DIED THERE"? UNTIL HERE MOSES WROTE; FROM HERE ON JOSHUA WROTE. R. MEIR SAYS: "AND MOSES WROTE THIS LAW" (31:9) — COULD MOSES HAVE GIVEN THE TORAH LACKING EVEN ONE LETTER? IT TEACHES THAT MOSES WROTE WHAT THE HOLY ONE TOLD HIM TO WRITE, AS "BARUCH SAID TO THEM: FROM HIS MOUTH HE RECITED TO ME" (Jeremiah 36:18). R. ELIEZER SAYS: A HEAVENLY VOICE WENT OUT THROUGH THE CAMP TWELVE MIL BY TWELVE MIL, PROCLAIMING: MOSES HAS DIED; SEMALYON SAID: "AND MOSES DIED THERE". WHENCE A PASSAGE FROM MOSES\' GRAVE TO THE FATHERS\'? "THERE" HERE AND "THERE THEY BURIED ABRAHAM AND SARAH HIS WIFE" (Genesis 49:31); SOME SAY MOSES DID NOT DIE BUT STANDS AND SERVES ABOVE — "THERE" HERE AND "AND HE WAS THERE WITH THE LORD" (Exodus 34:28). ({SP_(357, 28, "עד", "כאן", "כתב", "משה", "מכן", "ואילך", "כתב")} "until here Moses wrote; from here on wrote"; {SP_(357, 28, "אפשר", "שנתן", "משה", "את", "התורה", "כשהיא", "חסרה")} "could Moses have given the Torah lacking"; {SP_(357, 28, "לא", "מת", "משה", "אלא", "עומד", "ומשרת", "למעלה")} "Moses did not die but stands and serves above"): 31:9\'s WRITING AS R. MEIR\'S PROOF THAT THE WHOLE TORAH, its last verses too, was Moses\' hand at dictation (against from here Joshua wrote) — the dispute over the book\'s last eight verses (Babylonian Talmud Bava Batra 15a the testing shelf, cited); THE HEBREW\'S MARKER READS 31:24 where the quoted words are 31:9\'s (and Moses wrote this law; 31:24 says finished writing the words of this law) and the English cites 31:9 — the row seated at 31:9 by its own words (the third marker misprint among the nineteen, with 1:1 and 302:1); the row from the last piska (357, on 34:1-5) read here for 31:9, the piska not opened. Fresh.')
